WEB SOURCE (the specification) — components/forms/PillFilterBar.tsx
  A PURE, presentational single-select filter row implementing the WAI-ARIA Tabs pattern. Its only hook is
  `useId` (a stable tablist id for the per-tab element ids) — there is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise,
  and NO `t()` call (labels + ariaLabel arrive already-localised as props). Props:
    • items: PillItem[] — { key, label, icon?, count?, accent? (cyan|green|amber|red|purple|blue, def cyan),
      disabled? }
    • activeKey, onChange(key), ariaLabel, variant ('pills' | 'tabs', def 'pills'), scrollable (def true),
      className, testId.
  Behaviour ported verbatim:
    • enabledKeys = items.filter(!disabled).map(key); arrow nav skips disabled pills.
    • handleKeyDown: ArrowLeft/ArrowRight step ±1 and WRAP around enabledKeys ((idx+delta+n)%n); a disabled/absent
      active key is a no-op (idx === -1); Home → first, End → last; empty ring → no-op. moveFocus = onChange + focus.
    • roving tabindex (selected pill = tabIndex 0); selection follows focus.
    • pills variant: rounded chip, active fill (bg/15) + ring (/40) + leading dot; muted `(fmtInt(count))` suffix.
    • tabs variant: flat row, 2px accent bottom-border underline on the selected item; faint baseline border.
    • icon optional leading glyph; count rendered only when a number (count 0 → "(0)").
  Faithful-parity decision (logged, not hidden): because the source has NO data source, it has NO loading / error /
  stale / offline branch. Inventing such chrome would FABRICATE states the spec does not have, so this surface
  reproduces only the REAL branches — exactly as the accepted sibling presentational surfaces ActiveFilterChips
  (0147) and CurrencyInput (0150). REAL branches shipped: empty (friendly labelled empty state — never a blank box),
  `pills`, `tabs`, selected/unselected, disabled, icon ±, count ±, scrollable ±.
  i18n keys extracted from source: NONE (anonymous surface; labels + ariaLabel are caller props). The only
  facade-resolved native string is the empty-row body (`pillFilterBar.empty`).

